      "writtenOn": "2018-02-15T18:31:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure I understand. IPv6 is supported on cell. Today none of the calls throw due to range checking; it\u0027s all done through the callbacks, so there\u0027s no Exception throwing in the pattern.\n\nPreviously this line had 2 invalid arguments:\n1) the address\n2) the keepalive interval\n\nThus, it was testing the keepalive interval check (intentionally) and the order of the range checking (unintentionally). My intent here was to make this only test one thing because we don\u0027t want to care about the order of the range checks (do we?)?",
